    "updated_at": "2022-02-10T16:01:19Z",
    "body": "`activeCodePage` might help avoid the explicit ` StandardOutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8;` in the PowerShell init once all supported Windows versions can handle it.\r\nI think `longPathAware` might be nice to have, but internally physical paths are already handled as `\\\\?\\` paths. It might be interesting to see how long paths without the prefix interact with command spawning with executables that don't support `\\\\?\\` paths (#3582). By the way, PowerShell does have `longPathAware` set.",
