    "updated_at": "2022-02-10T17:13:00Z",
    "body": "Yep. Rust is using the `WriteConsoleW` trick so it can write Unicode to a console without having to change the output code page (Python 3 also does that BTW). https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/library/std/src/sys/windows/stdio.rs\r\n\r\nIt seems Rust always outputs UTF-8 for a non-console stdio, disregarding the legacy ANSI code page. So `activeCodePage` probably has no effect.\r\n\r\nFurther annoyance is that PowerShell doesn't seem to use the `$OutputEncoding` when reading from native processes but rather the console output code page, even for a process that uses `activeCoedPage` and that outputs UTF-8 it seems, which is what leads to needing the `Invoke-Native` hack as the builtin `Start-Process` cmdlet doesn't allow setting the output encoding.\r\n\r\nEncoding on Windows sucks so bad...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
